{"type": "FeatureCollection", "features": [{"type": "Feature", "properties": {"company": "Great Northern Railway", "line": "Great Northern: Crookston \u2013 Duluth", "id": "gn-fosston-bemidji-grandrapids", "color": "#1E6091", "mode": "intercity_rail", "avg_speed_kmh": 45, "speed_source": "estimated: typical GN branch-line service of the era; unsourced", "segments": [{"start": 1898, "end": 1950, "headway_min": 360, "note": "Built through Bemidji in summer 1898, extending an existing Crookston-Fosston line (Crookston was on GN's original main route north to Winnipeg) east through Bemidji to Deer River and Grand Rapids. In 1897 GN's Eastern Railway Company had acquired the separately-built Duluth, Superior and Western line running from Duluth toward Deer River, and extended it on to Fosston, completing one continuous route from the GN mainline at Crookston all the way to the port at Duluth. Bemidji owed its initial settlement and prosperity largely to this line. A grand 1913 depot (the last one commissioned by GN founder James J. Hill personally) replaced the original 1898 wooden station at Bemidji. Passenger service ended in 1950, 21 years before Amtrak existed. Frequency estimated, unsourced.", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Northern_Railway_(U.S."]}], "geometry_repairs": [{"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-96.6081167, 47.7739988], "to": [-95.751415, 47.5763481], "chord_mi": 42.36, "traced_mi": 45.4, "snap_m": [111, 104], "bridged_mi": 0.0, "osm_lines": ["BNSF Grand Forks Subdivision (35.88 mi)", "(abandoned) [abandoned] (9.52 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.0 km corridor, Dijkstra, simplified to 3.0 m"}, {"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-95.751415, 47.5763481], "to": [-94.8832791, 47.4723148], "